/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-017/great_expectations/docs/docusaurus/docs/oss/changelog.md:1157: [行の長さ 450 字。当たった 1 か所の前後 200 字] …When a password or secret contains a literal `$`, Great Expectations no longer includes the text following the `$` in the resulting missing-config-variable error message, so part of the secret is not leaked in logs. The error guidance also no longer points at the retired `$MY_CONFIG_VAR` substitution syntax. ([#11693](https://github.com/fivetran/great_expectations/pull/11693))…
/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-trade/2da9385f-4fe4-506a-be3d-78153c549662/scratchpad/cat8/venvs/8-017/great_expectations/docs/docusaurus/docs/oss/changelog.md:1179: - Config variable substitution errors no longer include text that follows a literal `$` in a password or secret, avoiding partial secret leakage, and their guidance no longer references the removed `$MY_CONFIG_VAR` syntax. ([#11693](https://github.com/fivetran/great_expectations/pull/11693))
